      "message": "You can search the code for `TestableSurfaceFlinger` - it\u0027s used by a variety of tests.\n\nBut I\u0027m not sure we have an existing test harness for this. @domlaskowski@google.com referenced I3488927d9a854a42432b7575d0daa14e61677c3e. (That\u0027s a change id, and Gerrit will turn it into a link, but it was submitted to Android\u0027s internal Gerrit, so AOSP Gerrit won\u0027t find anything. But you can find it in the `git log`.) It shows some test updates, but nothing that tests the new behavior.\n\nI notice that `TestableSurfaceFlinger.h` has `FakeHwcDisplayInjector`, which has a method that injects a `HWC2Display`, which seems to help for testing? This might hint at a way to go? (Dom, any thoughts?)\n\nGiven that we have no tests already, I might be fine with landing as-is, with the caveat that I cannot guarantee that we won\u0027t break it later. (A test would help prevent that!)",
